# Caddyfile, and workspaces' own domains beside it (rove#155): read instead of
# Caddyfile once compose.domains.yaml is (README.md, "워크스페이스 도메인").
#
# The service's own address is Caddyfile's, as it was. Any other host a
# browser asks for is a workspace's domain or nothing: before Caddy takes a
# certificate for one -- loads it, obtains it, renews it -- it asks the
# operator's entry point whether the host is a workspace's verified domain in
# use, and how often it may (`admin.ask`). A host nobody verified is never
# given one, and its handshake fails.
{
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://rove-admin:8082/internal/tls-ask
	}
	# More of Caddy's global options, from .env's ROVE_EDGE_OPTIONS: an e-mail
	# for the ACME account, to hear of a certificate that cannot be renewed
	# (`email ops@example.com`).
	{$ROVE_EDGE_OPTIONS:}
}

import Caddyfile

https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	import rove
}
